flickos-recovery (1.2) trixie; urgency=medium

  * Tests never run the installed recovery-helper: on a build computer
    with flickos-recovery installed, a test went through pkexec, asked
    for the password and failed the build.

 -- Jon <dvbondoy@gmail.com>  Sun, 11 Oct 2026 22:02:29 +0800

flickos-recovery (1.1) trixie; urgency=medium

  * The boot menu's Restore points (ADR-004): /etc/grub.d/42_flickos-
    recovery and the entries in /boot/grub/flickos-recovery.cfg, written
    after every change; started from one, the initramfs puts a writable
    layer in memory over it, and putting it back keeps it (restore
    points design, phase 2).
  * The start counter (ADR-005): flickos-recovery-start and -good
    services, GRUB reads it and starts the newest good restore point
    after 2 failed starts (auto-recover yes) or waits with it
    highlighted (no), never twice in a row; start keep|try-again, set
    auto-recover. The settings move to @snapshots, so putting back or a
    start from a restore point doesn't lose them.
  * notify: at login, started from a restore point, a notification says
    so; a click opens Settings' Restore Points page.

 -- Jon <dvbondoy@gmail.com>  Sat, 10 Oct 2026 17:24:52 +0800

flickos-recovery (1.0) trixie; urgency=medium

  * Restore points before every software change: the apt hook, list,
    create, delete, state, get/set enabled (restore points design, phase
    1).
  * Putting back: restore, plan, settle (a oneshot at the next start),
    apt refused until the restart, GRUB installed again from the
    restored system; recovery-helper and its polkit actions for Settings
    and for users (ADR-003).
  * A restore point is committed at once (btrfs filesystem sync): after
    a power cut early in an upgrade it was gone. The swap is committed
    before GRUB is installed again.
  * Nothing in a chroot: the installer's own apt runs (Calamares works
    in a chroot of the new system) made restore points of a half-
    installed system.

 -- Jon <dvbondoy@gmail.com>  Sat, 10 Oct 2026 14:38:42 +0800
